<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Sept aluminium exports 1.946 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Sept aluminium exports 1.946 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian exports of aluminium continued to soar on 1995 levels and were 1,946,000 tonnes over January-September, but September deliveries fell 17 percent on August levels, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The committee gave the following figures for metals exports and output-</p>
<p>		    RUSSIAN NON-FERROUS METALS EXPORTS</p>
<p>	     Jan-Sept 1996  pct change    Sept 1996, pct change-</p>
<p>		(tonnes)	yr/yr		mth/mth   yr/yr</p>
<p> Aluminium  1,946,000	+24.0	     -17.0     -5.0</p>
<p> Copper	 401,000	+24.0		-5.0     +1.0</p>
<p> Nickel	 118,000	 +9.0		+5.0     -6.0</p>
<p>		    RUSSIAN NON-FERROUS METALS OUTPUT</p>
<p>			  Jan-Oct 1996,     Oct 1996, pct change:</p>
<p>			  pct change	   mth/mth	yr/yr</p>
<p>			  yr/yr</p>
<p> Primary aluminium   +5.0		   +6.0	   +3.0</p>
<p> Alumina		 -2.0		   +5.0	   -6.0</p>
<p> Rolled aluminium   -39.0		  +10.0	  -19.0</p>
<p> Refined copper	+6.0		  +19.0	   +5.0</p>
<p> Copper Concentrate   0.0		    0.0	  -11.0</p>
<p> Nickel		  -5.0		   +4.0	  -11.0</p>
<p> Cobalt		  -5.0		   +8.0	  -36.0</p>
<p> Zinc		    +4.0		   +1.0	   +7.0</p>
<p> Gold (mined)	  -9.0		  -13.0	  +11.0</p>
<p>Note: The committee gave no absolute production or monthly export figures. Exports are to countries outside the Commonwealth of Independent States. The committee's export figures always lag production figures by one month. Monthly production levels can vary on seasonal factors.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
